                           <th>Conclusion and Recommendations based on this report and previous findings known to us:</th>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>Thyrotropin (TSH) is elevated above the reference range, which may indicate primary hypothyroidism or recovery from non-thyroidal illness. Correlation with clinical symptoms and further assessment of thyroid hormone levels (free T4, free T3) are recommended to clarify thyroid function status and guide management.</td>
